                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237520795",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199337545757",
                            "num_reviews": 8,
                            "playtime_forever": 9063,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 9063,
                            "last_played": 1791738973
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I’m coming into Persona 3 Reload as someone who never touched the original or the PSP version. My entry point to the series was Persona 5 Royal, and honestly, Reload is one of the best things that could’ve happened to newcomers like me. You don’t need any prior history with the franchise to get completely swept away by this game.\n\nWhat really hit me is how much heart this game has. The story, the characters, the music, the sense that your time with the SEES crew is slipping away day by day. It all builds into something that genuinely sticks with you. I got attached to this cast in a way I didn’t expect, and by the time the credits rolled, I felt hollow. Not because the game ended badly, but because it made me care so much that saying goodbye hurt. Very few games have done that to me.\n\nI’ve noticed a lot of longtime fans are weighed down by nostalgia, especially those who played the original or FES/Portable. I get it, those versions mean a lot to people. But as someone with no baggage, I can say that Reload stands on its own as a fantastic experience. And speaking of the female protagonist, I can’t help but wonder how much more special this would’ve been with her route included. Even without ever playing the older versions, I’m curious how that would’ve played out here. It would’ve made an already great game even better.\n\nIf you’re coming from Persona 5 and wondering whether to jump into 3, don’t hesitate. Play it. Just be ready for the emptiness afterward.\n\nRating: 9/10",
